 <!-- The Hook -->
 <div class="bg-brandBlue/5 border-l-4 border-brandOrange p-6 rounded-r-xl mb-8 speakable">
 <p class="text-lg text-slate-700 italic">In March 2026, an EU importer's entire container of GaN chargers was seized at Rotterdam — not because the products failed testing, but because the CE certificate their factory provided listed a testing lab that didn't exist. The lab logo was photoshopped onto a template. Three months and €8,400 in storage fees later, the shipment was destroyed. Fake or invalid certification documents are the single most expensive oversight in OEM charger importing — and they're easier to catch than most buyers think. This guide covers the 5 database lookups and visual checks that take under 10 minutes but can save you a seized shipment.</p>
 </div>

  </div>
 </div>

