<!-- Section 1: US Market -->
 <section id="us-market" class="mb-16">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">1. US Market: OEM Charger Certifications &amp; Requirements</h2>

 <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 uppercase mb-3">UL 62368-1: Safety (Effectively Mandatory)</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">Technically voluntary under federal law, UL certification is required by Amazon, Walmart, and Best Buy to list chargers. Amazon now enforces UL test reports for chargers and power adapters. <a href="https://www.ul.com/resources/ul-62368-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">UL 62368-1</a> has fully replaced UL 60950-1. ETL and CSA are accepted alternatives. For a deeper look at <a href="/blog/charger-safety-standards" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange">charger safety standards</a>, see our dedicated guide.</p>

 <h3 class="font-black text-slate-900 uppercase mb-3">FCC Part 15B: EMC (Mandatory)</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">Every charger with a switching power supply must comply with <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-A/part-15" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FCC Part 15</a> regulations. Two paths exist:</p>
 <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-6">
 <table class="w-full border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
 <thead class="bg-brandBlue text-white">
 <tr><th class="text-left p-4 font-black uppercase text-sm">Method</th><th class="text-left p-4 font-black uppercase text-sm">When to Use</th><th class="text-left p-4 font-black uppercase text-sm">Cost Range</th></tr>
 </thead>
 <tbody>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200"><td class="p-4 font-bold">SDoC (Self-Declaration)</td><td class="p-4">Basic chargers, no wireless</td><td class="p-4 text-brandBlue font-bold">$500-$1,200</td></tr>
 <tr><td class="p-4 font-bold">Full Certification (FCC ID)</td><td class="p-4">Wi-Fi/Bluetooth chargers</td><td class="p-4 text-brandBlue font-bold">$3,000-$6,000</td></tr>
 </tbody>
 </table>
 </div>
 <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">FCC has <strong>no mutual recognition</strong> with CE. Separate testing is always required.</p>

 <div class="mt-6 mb-6">
 <img src="/image/blog/car-charger-guide/car-charger-voltage-current-test.webp" alt="FCC Part 15B compliance testing: PD 3.1 charger output voltage and current measurement on Keysight multimeter during OEM certification testing" title="FCC Part 15B EMC Compliance Testing, WOWOHCOOL Inline QC" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg">
