 <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">US and EU charger certification differs across seven dimensions that OEM importers must navigate. The fundamental difference: <strong>the US requires third-party NRTL testing</strong> (UL/ETL) for safety certification at $3,000-$8,000 and 8-12 weeks, while the <strong>EU uses manufacturer self-declaration</strong> under CE marking at $1,500-$4,000 and 4-10 weeks. US certification costs roughly twice as much but is required by Amazon and major retailers; EU certification is less expensive upfront but the importer bears full legal responsibility for compliance verification and market surveillance.</p>
